    "result_text": "Done. The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement was to reject owner creation (and updates) with **400** when the email domain is on a disposable-domain blocklist.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `NormalizeOwnerEmail.java` (the single email step shared by both `POST /api/owners` and `PUT /api/owners/{ownerId}`):\n- Added a `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS` set (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n- After the existing syntax check, it extracts the lower-cased domain (after `@`) and throws `InvalidEmailException` when it's on the blocklist.\n\nThis reuses the existing `InvalidEmailException` \u2192 `InvalidEmailExceptionHandler` escalation, which already responds `400`, so no new YAML or handler was needed. The check is case-insensitive (domain is lower-cased first) and placed in the normalize step so it's governed by the pipeline transaction and runs for both endpoints.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` (POST with `x@mailinator.com` \u2192 400) passes, and the full test suite is green.",
